{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/yd52ep","slide":6,"text":"Describe the dual-write gap. The transfer, balance changes, and outbox row commit together in PostgreSQL. A publisher later sends the event. If it crashes after Kafka accepts the event but before marking the row delivered, it may publish again. That is at-least-once delivery, so consumers must be idempotent. Debezium CDC is a roadmap option, not a free reliability upgrade."}
