{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/5cnmd83a","slide":7,"bbox":[76,458,1128,1]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/4be5432p","slide":7,"text":"Token bucket policy","textPreview":"Token bucket policy","textChars":19,"textLines":1,"bbox":[80,489,258,29]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/3m9onil8","slide":7,"text":"Allows short bursts while limiting average request rate. Apply per user or client.","textPreview":"Allows short bursts while limiting average request rate. Apply per user or client.","textChars":82,"textLines":1,"bbox":[80,530,475,54]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/2lgnexk3","slide":7,"text":"Redis outage policy","textPreview":"Redis outage policy","textChars":19,"textLines":1,"bbox":[654,489,258,29]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/y1k7mh4b","slide":7,"text":"Fail open favors availability. Fail closed protects capacity but can reject valid requests.","textPreview":"Fail open favors availability. Fail closed protects capacity but can reject valid requests.","textChars":91,"textLines":1,"bbox":[654,530,495,54]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/iddnzb","slide":7,"text":"Walk through the filter chain: validate token signature and claims, then authorize the caller against the source wallet. Rate limiting is a separate resilience control. A token bucket permits bursts while bounding the long-run rate. Distributed counters require atomic Redis operations and a deliberate fail-open or fail-closed policy."}
