{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/k3u5crep","slide":8,"text":"Report workload, hardware, concurrency, and p95/p99 latency with any throughput result.","textPreview":"Report workload, hardware, concurrency, and p95/p99 latency with any throughput result.","textChars":87,"textLines":1,"bbox":[78,631,1100,27]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/5kmx4l","slide":8,"text":"Describe the test pyramid and stress that unit tests alone cannot validate PostgreSQL row locking. Run concurrency scenarios against the database engine used by the service. Assert value conservation and balance bounds. No benchmark result is claimed in this deck; report throughput only after measuring a specified workload, hardware, pool size, and latency percentiles."}
