{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/oj6tk3ax","slide":9,"text":"Horizontal API scaling does not remove contention on shared account rows.","textPreview":"Horizontal API scaling does not remove contention on shared account rows.","textChars":73,"textLines":1,"bbox":[78,603,1100,36]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/6kafac","slide":9,"text":"Be explicit that database row locking protects correctness but constrains writes to hot accounts. Horizontal API scaling helps stateless request handling, not conflicting updates to one row. CDC can lower polling overhead but adds operational dependencies. Sharding is a later option because cross-shard transfers become much harder to coordinate atomically."}
